  "solution": "Given equation: 13 + 18 × 6 – 30 ÷ 6 = –90\n\nAfter interchanging the signs, we get:\n\n1. −, ÷\n\n13 + 18 × __**6 ÷ 30**__ - 6 = –90\n\n⇒ 13 + __**18 × 0.2**__ - 6 = –90\n\n⇒ __**13 + 3.6**__ - 6 = –90\n\n⇒ 16.6 - 6 = –90\n\n⇒ 10.6 ≠ -90\n\n2. ×, ÷\n\n13 + __**18 ÷ 6**__ – 30 × 6 = –90\n\n⇒ 13 + 3 – __**30 **____**×**____** 6**__ = –90\n\n⇒ __**13 + 3**__ - 180 = -90\n\n⇒ 16 - 180 = -90\n\n⇒ -164 ≠ -90\n\n3. +, −\n\n13 - 18 × 6 + __**30 ÷ 6**__ = –90\n\n⇒ 13 - __**18 × 6**__ + 5 = –90\n\n⇒ __**13**__ - 108 __**+**____** 5**__ = –90\n\n⇒ 18 - 108 = -90\n\n⇒ -90 = -90\n\n4. +, ×\n\n13 × 18 + 6 – **__30 ÷ 6__** = –90\n\n⇒ __**13 **____**×**____** 18**__ + 6 – 5 = –90\n\n⇒ __**234**____** + 6**__ – 5 = –90\n\n⇒ 240 – 5 = –90\n\n⇒ 235 ≠ –90\n\nHence, '**+, −**' is the correct answer.",
